    "label": "[N085171], Technical Note, Francis Robbins Upton, October 22nd, 1879",
    "metadata": [
        {
            "label": "Title",
            "value": "[N085171], Technical Note, Francis Robbins Upton, October 22nd, 1879"
        },
        {
            "label": "Editor's Notes",
            "value": "Carbon spirals and threads.  Trying to make a lamp of a carbonized thread.  100 ohms can be made from an inch of .010 inch thread.  A thread with 45 ohms resistance when cold was brought up in a high vacuum to 4 candles about.  It remained constant for two or three hours and then the resistance seemed to concentrate in one spot.  Resistance cold 800 ohms; notes and calcs on thread lamp power requirements follow, also thread carbonized with lampblack"
        },
        {
            "label": "Author",
            "value": "Upton, Francis Robbins"
        },
        {
            "label": "Date",
            "value": "1879-10-22"
        },
        {
            "label": "Type",
            "value": "Technical Note"
        },
        {
            "label": "Subject",
            "value": [
                "Carbon, coal, glass, ceramics",
                "Incandescent lamp",
                "Vacuum and glass bulb"
            ]
        },
